cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code in your research, please cite this software.
type: software
title: "Mathematical epidemiological analysis of the 2025-2026 measles outbreaks that ended Canada's 27 Year Measles Elimination status"
authors:
  - family-names: Korosec
    given-names: Chapin S.
abstract: >-
  This github contains R scripts for fitting and analysing SEIR models of five provincial
  measles waves: Ontario 2025, Alberta 2025 and 2026, and Manitoba
  2025 and 2026. The workflow uses Monolix through lixoftConnectors
  for parameter estimation and initial infectious seed-size profiling,
  with weekly time units, BIC-based model comparison, sensitivity
  analyses of latent and infectious periods, and uncertainty propagation.
  Outputs include effective reproduction numbers, effective susceptible
  population sizes, initial exponential growth rates, doubling times,
  peak full widths at half maximum, and manuscript figures and tables.
keywords:
  - measles
  - mathematical epidemiology
  - SEIR
  - parameter estimation
  - Monolix
  - Canada
